Embedded React: clip Text, TextInput and span strings at a character boundary.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/include/er_scene.h, engine/scene/compositor.c
and bridges/quickjs/native_ui_bridge.c. Not yet proposed upstream.

A nested Text's span strings were cut at 63 bytes (ER_SPAN_TEXT_MAX) with a
plain byte count, so a CJK, Devanagari or Bengali segment could end in half a
UTF-8 sequence; the bridge cut Text strings at 255 bytes (ER_TEXT_MAX) the same
way before the engine dropped the partial sequence. The new er_utf8_clip()
returns the longest prefix within a byte limit that ends at a character
boundary and, when text is dropped, does not separate a combining mark, joiner
or conjunct consonant (after a virama) from the character it belongs to. The
bridge's string props, span strings, er_node_set_props(),
er_node_set_text_spans() and er_text_input_set_text() copy through it. The
limits stay as they are: a longer span would grow every node, since text
properties are the largest member of the node's property union.

